<figure class="wal-progress" aria-labelledby="r36-progress-title" data-wal-progress>
 <p class="figure-title" id="r36-progress-title">Figure 1 · Three positions, one commit</p>
 <p class="model-note">Illustrative WAL sequence. Each box is a record group, not a fixed number of bytes.</p>
 <div class="record-key"><span>Earlier</span><span>Purchase</span><span>Commit</span></div>
 <div class="lanes" role="img" aria-label="WAL insertion, file write and durable flush progressing through the same record groups" aria-describedby="r36-progress-text">
  {['Inserted','Written','Flushed'].map((label,row)=><div class="lane"><strong>{label}</strong><div class="track">{[0,1,2].map(col=><span data-cell={`${row}-${col}`} class:list={{reached:col===0}}>{col===0?'✓':'·'}</span>)}</div></div>)}
 </div>
 <p class="outcome" data-live data-outcome>Application: waiting · purchase not yet committed</p>
 <p id="r36-progress-text" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Only earlier history is durable. Order 103 has not been written.</p>
 <div class="options"><label>Commit mode <select data-mode><option value="on">on: wait for flush</option><option value="off">off: reply before flush</option></select></label></div>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="WAL progress playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span></div>
 <div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 <figcaption>Step through the default, then choose <em>off</em> and reset. The latter cuts the model before any later writer flushes this commit. Real background writes can advance sooner; the figure exposes the allowed loss, rather than predicting when a crash will land.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>Read the two paths as text</summary><p>With on: insert purchase records; insert commit record; write WAL to the file; flush WAL; acknowledge. The heap pages may still be old. With off: insert purchase and commit; acknowledge; crash before their WAL is flushed; recover earlier history. An actual process crash may retain file writes in the operating system's cache, so the loss path assumes these records have not reached that cache either.</p></details>
</figure>
<style>
.wal-progress{margin:2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);font: .9rem/1.55 var(--font-sans)}.wal-progress .figure-title{margin:0 0 .8rem;font-size:1.1rem}.model-note{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.record-key{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-left:6rem;gap:.4rem;text-align:center;font-size:.8rem}.lane{display:grid;grid-template-columns:5.6rem 1fr;gap:.4rem;align-items:center;margin:.5rem 0}.track{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:.4rem}.track span{border:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary);text-align:center;padding:.55rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.track .reached{border:1px solid var(--color-accent);background:var(--color-accent);color:var(--color-surface)}.outcome{border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:.8rem 0;margin-top:1rem}.options select{max-width:100%;font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);padding:.4rem}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;align-items:center;margin:.8rem 0}.controls button{font:inherit;padding:.45rem .65rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.2rem;cursor:pointer}.controls button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}.controls button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}[data-hold]{height:3px;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;width:0;height:100%;background:var(--color-accent)}figcaption{margin:1rem 0;font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details p{margin-top:.7rem}
</style>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-wal-progress]')){
 const mode=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mode]')!;
 const normal=[{p:[0,0,0],a:'waiting · purchase not yet committed',t:'Only earlier history is durable. Order 103 has not been written.'},{p:[1,0,0],a:'waiting · changes in memory',t:'The purchase changes pages in shared buffers and appends WAL. Inserted has advanced, but written and flushed have not.'},{p:[2,0,0],a:'waiting · commit record inserted',t:'The commit record follows the purchase records. Insertion into WAL buffers alone does not meet the normal acknowledgement promise.'},{p:[2,2,0],a:'waiting · WAL handed to the operating system',t:'Written reaches the commit. The operating system may still hold these bytes in volatile cache.'},{p:[2,2,2],a:'waiting · commit recoverable locally',t:'The flush completes through the commit record. Recovery has enough durable WAL even if the heap pages remain old.'},{p:[2,2,2],a:'success · order 103 confirmed',t:'Only now does the normal commit reply. The page writers can finish separately; no checkpoint is needed for this reply.'}];
 const relaxed=[normal[0],normal[1],{...normal[2],a:'success · reply before flush',t:'With synchronous_commit off, the commit can be acknowledged now. Other sessions can see the purchase, although its WAL has not yet been written or flushed.'},{p:[0,0,0],a:'success was heard · process crashes',t:'In this allowed cut, neither the operating system nor durable storage received the new records. Losing PostgreSQL memory removes the purchase and commit records.'},{p:[0,0,0],a:'earlier history recovered · confirmation lost',t:'Recovery has no surviving commit record for the purchase. The database is consistent, but order 103 is absent despite the earlier success reply.'}];
 const states=()=>mode.value==='on'?normal:relaxed;
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>states().length,draw:(n:number)=>{const s=states()[n];root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cell]').forEach(c=>{const [r,k]=c.dataset.cell!.split('-').map(Number);const yes=k<=s.p[r];c.classList.toggle('reached',yes);c.textContent=yes?'✓':'·';});root.querySelector('[data-outcome]')!.textContent='Application: '+s.a;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.t;}});
 mode.addEventListener('change',()=>{root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click();player.render();});
}
</script>
